cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MeghBhed, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "MeghBhed: Mapping flooding under tree cover with NISAR L-band radar"
abstract: >-
  MeghBhed (মেঘভেদ, "piercing the clouds") is Team Last_Call's entry to the
  NASA International Space Apps Challenge 2026 ("Dancing with the SARs").
  It plans to use NASA-ISRO NISAR L-band radar (L2 GCOV) to detect flooding
  under tree cover, where C-band flood maps such as OPERA DSWx-S1 are largely
  blind, and to estimate the number of people affected per upazila using
  WorldPop. The first study area is Chattogram and Feni districts, Bangladesh,
  during the July 2026 floods. A second layer flags slopes with possible
  landslides for ground checks. Status: concept; the build takes place at the
  hackathon in November 2026.
